An overview of OpenRouter’s API

Copy pageCopy page

OpenRouter’s request and response schemas are very similar to OpenAI’s APIs, with a few small differences. At a high level, **OpenRouter normalizes the schema across models and providers** so you only need to learn one. OpenRouter supports two request shapes: the [Responses API](https://openrouter.ai/docs/api_reference/responses/overview) (`POST /api/v1/responses`) and the Chat Completions API (`POST /api/v1/chat/completions`). Where this page shows both, the Responses API comes first. The TypeScript schemas below describe Chat Completions; the Responses API schema is in the [Responses API reference](https://openrouter.ai/docs/api_reference/responses/overview).

## 

[​

](https://openrouter.ai/docs/api_reference/overview#openapi-specification)

OpenAPI specification

The complete OpenRouter API is documented using the OpenAPI specification. You can access the specification in either YAML or JSON format:

*   **YAML**: [https://openrouter.ai/openapi.yaml](https://openrouter.ai/openapi.yaml)
*   **JSON**: [https://openrouter.ai/openapi.json](https://openrouter.ai/openapi.json)

These specifications can be used with tools like [Swagger UI](https://swagger.io/tools/swagger-ui/), [Postman](https://www.postman.com/), or any OpenAPI-compatible code generator to explore the API or generate client libraries.

